The Illinois DHS System Failure (January 2026)
​This is a very recent "headline" incident that highlights the human element in security.
​The Incident: A misconfigured system at the Illinois Department of Human Services exposed sensitive public assistance data online.
​The Impact: Combined with a similar case in Minnesota around the same time, nearly one million people had their personal and financial information exposed.
​The Lesson: It wasn't a sophisticated zero-day exploit; it was a failure in applying proper access restrictions to a public-facing system.
